{"id":"mahabharata-4-056","work":"mahabharata","part":4,"partName":"विराटपर्व","partNameEn":"Virata Parva","unit":56,"title":"षट्पञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 56 · Arjuna turns towards Bhishma","summary":{"en":"After defeating Karna, Arjuna asks Uttara to drive towards Bhishma's palm-tree banner, promising to uproot the forest of Dhritarashtra's sons. Uttara, awed and wounded, drives on, and Arjuna's arrows fill every quarter of the sky.","kn":"ಕರ್ಣನನ್ನು ಸೋಲಿಸಿದ ಮೇಲೆ ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರಪುತ್ರರ ಕಾಡನ್ನು ಕಿತ್ತೊಗೆಯುವೆನೆಂದು ಹೇಳಿ ಭೀಷ್ಮನ ತಾಳಧ್ವಜದತ್ತ ರಥ ನಡೆಸೆಂದು ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಉತ್ತರನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಬೆರಗಾದ ಗಾಯಗೊಂಡ ಉತ್ತರನು ಮುಂದೆ ಸಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಬಾಣಗಳು ಆಕಾಶದ ಎಲ್ಲ ದಿಕ್ಕುಗಳನ್ನು ತುಂಬುತ್ತವೆ.","hi":"कर्ण को हराकर अर्जुन उत्तर से भीष्म की ताल-ध्वजा की ओर रथ ले चलने को कहते हैं और धृतराष्ट्र-पुत्रों के वन को उखाड़ फेंकने का वचन देते हैं। विस्मित और घायल उत्तर आगे बढ़ता है, और अर्जुन के बाण आकाश की हर दिशा भर देते हैं।","te":"కర్ణుని ఓడించిన తర్వాత ధృతరాష్ట్రపుత్రుల అడవిని పెకలిస్తానని చెప్పి భీష్ముని తాళధ్వజం వైపు రథం నడపమని అర్జునుడు ఉత్తరునికి చెబుతాడు. ఆశ్చర్యపోయి గాయపడిన ఉత్తరుడు ముందుకు సాగుతాడు, అర్జునుని బాణాలు ఆకాశపు అన్ని దిక్కులనూ నింపుతాయి.","ta":"கர்ணனை வென்ற பின் த்ருதராஷ்டிர மைந்தர்களின் காட்டைப் பிடுங்கி எறிவேன் என்று சொல்லிப் பீஷ்மரின் பனைமரக் கொடியை நோக்கித் தேரைச் செலுத்துமாறு அர்ஜுனன் உத்தரனிடம் சொல்கிறான். வியந்து காயமுற்ற உத்தரன் தொடர்ந்து செலுத்த, அர்ஜுனனின் அம்புகள் வானின் எல்லாத் திசைகளையும் நிறைக்கின்றன.","ml":"കർണ്ണനെ തോൽപ്പിച്ചശേഷം, ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രപുത്രന്മാരുടെ വനം പിഴുതെറിയുമെന്ന് വാക്കുനൽകി, ഭീഷ്മരുടെ താലധ്വജത്തിന് നേരെ തെളിക്കാൻ അർജുനൻ ഉത്തരനോട് പറയുന്നു. വിസ്മയിച്ചും മുറിവേറ്റും ഉത്തരൻ തെളിക്കുന്നു; അർജുനന്റെ അമ്പുകൾ ആകാശത്തിന്റെ എല്ലാ ദിക്കുകളും നിറയ്ക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 4.56; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Dec  1 2011","sections":[{"title":"गोग्रहणपर्व","titleEn":"Gograhana Parva (The cattle raid)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो वैकर्तनं जित्वा पार्थो वैराटिमब्रवीत् ।\nएतन्मां प्रापयानीकं यत्र तालो हिरण्मयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having defeated Karna, son of Vikartana, Partha said to Virata's son, \"Take me to that division where the golden palm banner is."}},{"n":2,"text":"अत्र शांतनवो भीष्मो रथेऽस्माकं पितामहः ।\nकाङ्क्षमाणो मया युद्धं तिष्ठत्यमरदर्शनः ।\nआदास्याम्यहमेतस्य धनुर्ज्यामपि चाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"There in his chariot stands Bhishma son of Shantanu, our grandfather, godlike to see, wanting to fight me. I will take his bow and even its string in battle."}},{"n":3,"text":"अस्यन्तं दिव्यमस्त्रं मां चित्रमद्य निशामय ।\nशतह्रदामिवायान्तीं स्तनयित्नोरिवाम्बरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Now watch my wondrous divine weapon as I shoot, coming like lightning in a cloud in the sky."}},{"n":4,"text":"सुवर्णपृष्ठं गाण्डीवं द्रक्ष्यन्ति कुरवो मम ।\nदक्षिणेनाथ वामेन कतरेण स्विदस्यति ।\nइति मां संगताः सर्वे तर्कयिष्यन्ति शत्रवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kurus will see my gold-backed Gandiva; \"Which hand does he shoot with, right or left?\" all the enemies gathered will wonder about me."}},{"n":5,"text":"शोणितोदां रथावर्तां नागनक्रां दुरत्ययाम् ।\nनदीं प्रस्यन्दयिष्यामि परलोकप्रवाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will make a river flow with blood for water, chariots for whirlpools, elephants for crocodiles, hard to cross and carrying toward the next world."}},{"n":6,"text":"पाणिपादशिरःपृष्ठबाहुशाखानिरन्तरम् ।\nवनं कुरूणां छेत्स्यामि भल्लैः संनतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With smooth-jointed spear arrows I will cut down the forest of the Kurus, thick with hands, feet, heads, backs, arms and branches."}},{"n":7,"text":"जयतः कौरवीं सेनामेकस्य मम धन्विनः ।\nशतं मार्गा भविष्यन्ति पावकस्येव कानने ।\nमया चक्रमिवाविद्धं सैन्यं द्रक्ष्यसि केवलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As I, a single archer, conquer the Kaurava army, there will be a hundred paths like those of fire in a forest. You will see the army whirled around by me like a wheel."}},{"n":8,"text":"असंभ्रान्तो रथे तिष्ठ समेषु विषमेषु च ।\nदिवमावृत्य तिष्ठन्तं गिरिं भेत्स्यामि धारिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Stay in your chariot unflustered on level ground and rough; I will split with showers of arrows the mountain that stands covering the sky."}},{"n":9,"text":"अहमिन्द्रस्य वचनात्संग्रामेऽभ्यहनं पुरा ।\nपौलोमान्कालखञ्जांश्च सहस्राणि शतानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago, at Indra's command, I killed in battle the Paulomas and Kalakhanjas, thousands and hundreds of them."}},{"n":10,"text":"अहमिन्द्राद्दृढां मुष्टिं ब्रह्मणः कृतहस्तताम् ।\nप्रगाढं तुमुलं चित्रमतिविद्धं प्रजापतेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From Indra I have a firm grip, from Brahma a skilled hand, and from Prajapati a deep, tumultuous and wondrous aim."}},{"n":11,"text":"अहं पारे समुद्रस्य हिरण्यपुरमारुजम् ।\nजित्वा षष्टिसहस्राणि रथिनामुग्रधन्विनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Across the sea I broke Hiranyapura after conquering sixty thousand fierce-bowed charioteers."}},{"n":12,"text":"ध्वजवृक्षं पत्तितृणं रथसिंहगणायुतम् ।\nवनमादीपयिष्यामि कुरूणामस्त्रतेजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the fire of my weapons I will set ablaze the forest of the Kurus, with banners for trees, foot soldiers for grass and herds of chariot-lions."}},{"n":13,"text":"तानहं रथनीडेभ्यः शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ।\nएकः संकालयिष्यामि वज्रपाणिरिवासुरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Alone I will drive them from their chariot-nests with smooth-jointed arrows, like the thunderbolt-wielder driving the asuras."}},{"n":14,"text":"रौद्रं रुद्रादहं ह्यस्त्रं वारुणं वरुणादपि ।\nअस्त्रमाग्नेयमग्नेश्च वायव्यं मातरिश्वनः ।\nवज्रादीनि तथास्त्राणि शक्रादहमवाप्तवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have gained the Raudra weapon from Rudra, the Varuna from Varuna, the Agneya from Agni, the Vayavya from the wind, and thunderbolt and other weapons from Shakra."}},{"n":15,"text":"धार्तराष्ट्रवनं घोरं नरसिंहाभिरक्षितम् ।\nअहमुत्पाटयिष्यामि वैराटे व्येतु ते भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will uproot the terrible forest of Dhritarashtra's sons, guarded by lions among men. Let your fear go, son of Virata.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"एवमाश्वासितस्तेन वैराटिः सव्यसाचिना ।\nव्यगाहत रथानीकं भीमं भीष्मस्य धीमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Comforted so by Savyasachin, Virata's son plunged into the dreadful chariot host of the wise Bhishma."}},{"n":17,"text":"तमायान्तं महाबाहुं जिगीषन्तं रणे परान् ।\nअभ्यवारयदव्यग्रः क्रूरकर्मा धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the mighty-armed Dhananjaya came, eager to defeat enemies in battle, the cruel-acting Bhishma calmly stopped him."}},{"n":18,"text":"तं चित्रमाल्याभरणाः कृतविद्या मनस्विनः ।\nआगच्छन्भीमधन्वानं मौर्वीं पर्यस्य बाहुभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The accomplished and spirited men with colorful garlands and ornaments came, looping bowstrings on their arms, against that terrible archer."}},{"n":19,"text":"दुःशासनो विकर्णश्च दुःसहोऽथ विविंशतिः ।\nआगत्य भीमधन्वानं बीभत्सुं पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duhshasana, Vikarna, Duhsaha and Vivimshati came and surrounded Bibhatsu of the fearsome bow."}},{"n":20,"text":"दुःशासनस्तु भल्लेन विद्ध्वा वैराटिमुत्तरम् ।\nद्वितीयेनार्जुनं वीरः प्रत्यविध्यत्स्तनान्तरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duhshasana pierced Virata's son Uttara with a spear-arrow and with a second hit Arjuna between the breasts."}},{"n":21,"text":"तस्य जिष्णुरुपावृत्य पृथुधारेण कार्मुकम् ।\nचकर्त गार्ध्रपत्रेण जातरूपपरिष्कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jishnu, turning, cut his gold-decorated bow with a broad-edged vulture-feathered arrow."}},{"n":22,"text":"अथैनं पञ्चभिः पश्चात्प्रत्यविध्यत्स्तनान्तरे ।\nसोऽपयातो रणं हित्वा पार्थबाणप्रपीडितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he struck him with five more arrows between the breasts, and Duhshasana, tormented by Partha's arrows, left the battle."}},{"n":23,"text":"तं विकर्णः शरैस्तीक्ष्णैर्गार्ध्रपत्रैरजिह्मगैः ।\nविव्याध परवीरघ्नमर्जुनं धृतराष्ट्रजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vikarna, a son of Dhritarashtra, pierced Arjuna, killer of enemy heroes, with sharp, straight-flying, vulture-feathered arrows."}},{"n":24,"text":"ततस्तमपि कौन्तेयः शरेणानतपर्वणा ।\nललाटेऽभ्यहनत्तूर्णं स विद्धः प्रापतद्रथात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kunti's son quickly struck him too on the forehead with a smooth-jointed arrow, and pierced, Vikarna fell from his chariot."}},{"n":25,"text":"ततः पार्थमभिद्रुत्य दुःसहः सविविंशतिः ।\nअवाकिरच्छरैस्तीक्ष्णैः परीप्सन्भ्रातरं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Duhsaha and Vivimshati attacked Partha and showered him with sharp arrows, trying to save their brother in the battle."}},{"n":26,"text":"तावुभौ गार्ध्रपत्राभ्यां निशिताभ्यां धनंजयः ।\nविद्ध्वा युगपदव्यग्रस्तयोर्वाहानसूदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya, calm, pierced the two of them together with sharp vulture-feathered arrows and killed their horses."}},{"n":27,"text":"तौ हताश्वौ विविद्धाङ्गौ धृतराष्ट्रात्मजावुभौ ।\nअभिपत्य रथैरन्यैरपनीतौ पदानुगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Both sons of Dhritarashtra, with horses killed and bodies wounded, were carried off by their followers on other chariots."}},{"n":28,"text":"सर्वा दिशश्चाभ्यपतद्बीभत्सुरपराजितः ।\nकिरीटमाली कौन्तेयो लब्धलक्षो महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The undefeated Bibhatsu, the mighty son of Kunti, crowned and with his aim fixed, then rushed in all directions."}}]}]}